{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/987583-when-did-shadow-names-become-common","id":987583,"title":"When did Shadow Names become common?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-14T20:38:32-07:00","id":987583,"title":"When did Shadow Names become common?","content":"As the thread topic. I'm beginning the ground work on a To the Strongest chronicle for my local lads and I was wondering when Shadow Names began being used among Mages. If there's a mention in Dark Eras, I apologise for missing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T20:41:54-07:00","id":987585,"title":"","content":"Probably about four seconds after the first Mastigos realized how sympathy works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T21:38:52-07:00","id":987598,"title":"","content":"Which would have made him the fastest to figure it out, but an Acanthus went back and figured it out first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T22:07:32-07:00","id":987611,"title":"","content":"They were using Shadow Names back in the Neolithic, and then even earlier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T22:19:32-07:00","id":987617,"title":"","content":"Hello there, I'm your friendly neighbourhood Anthropology student! As it just so happens, I'm currently taking a course called &quot;Myth, Magic, and Shamanism&quot; which focuses on different approaches in various cultures to the sacred supernatural, societal rituals, and how those things intersect. Conveniently, it's turning me into a significantly better Mage player because when you sit in this mindset for a while you can tease apart symbols in ritual with absolutely laughable ease. One of our in-class assignments was to come up with a myth and a ritual based on said myth, and our prof plucked at least half a dozen of what <b>Mage</b> would term Yantras out of the invented rituals with ease.<br /> <br /> The Awakened are, by and large, what anthropological terminology would classify as a Shaman. Technically speaking, a Shaman is a part-time religious specialist whose position and authority in a society is predicated on personal contact and relationship with the sacred supernatural, demonstrated through effective rituals. Some seek out the calling of Shaman, but most are chosen by different spiritual beings, or called in a dream. Usually these new Shamans are thoroughly unhappy about this, as they know from cultural immersion in this topic that being a Shaman is dangerous work that could potentially involve death and/or having their soul eaten if things go badly. Nonetheless, they eventually find themselves a teacher who trains them in the ways of their art, these relationships are often volatile, as the student typically doesn't want to be there, and the master usually does't like the student, but they persist and eventually the Shaman is trained and initiated in a ritual that involves symbolic death and resurrection, making the Shaman a new person. Shamans are 'on call' in the sense that they're basically a normal member of their social group, doing normal person things, and then the supernatural intrudes on everyday life and somebody needs a divination, or a healing, or a soul needs to be stolen back from a spirit or angry ghost, and <i>then </i>the Shaman hat comes on. Generally, to help separate their 'work' life from their 'civilian' life, these Shamans have ritual personas, letting the spirits and the people know when they're on the clock.<br /> <br /> So, from a cultural stand-point, Shadow Names are hard-baked into the idea of 'Magic Practitioner as Member of Society' (Note Important Capital Letters, Wizards Like Important Capital Letters) and in <b>Mage: The Awakening </b>this is additionally good practice due to the metaphysical weirdness of the long-term Nimbus, all the awful things Sympathetic magic can do to you (a real-world concern for serious practitioners as well, and an equally solid motivation behind the person), and a way of letting others- Awakened or otherwise -know you're on the clock, as it were.<br /> <br /> <b>TLDR- </b>Even in the real world, Shadow Names are a thing for those who practice magic in their communities. The idea and the mantle of Practitioner of the Art as a separate person from Bob-who-knows-some-Magic go hand-in-hand as far back as anyone can tell, even to shamanistic cave drawings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T22:43:26-07:00","id":987628,"title":"","content":"&quot;No, call me Big Sky Fire. Much grander.&quot;<br /> &quot;Yes! I will be Roaring Winds.&quot;<br /> &quot;Call me Ravaging Swarm.&quot;<br /> &quot;I'll be Deer Cat.&quot;<br /> &quot;Wait, why do <i>I</i> have to be Bad Fishing?&quot; <br /> &quot;Because you were slow and passive, Fishing.&quot;<br /> <br /> Bonus for you: The first theme cabal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T23:52:11-07:00","id":987647,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the information folks. Curious, does anyone know where I could grab some inspiration for Hellenistic period Shadow Names then? Obviously I can raid Greek mythology, anything else spring to mind though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T06:29:30-07:00","id":987719,"title":"","content":"I imagine there's more than one fan of Plato. They could either borrow from his name or any terminology he came up with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T08:30:35-07:00","id":987767,"title":"","content":"Antiquity Hellenism you mean? If so, don't pick a deity name unless the character is prone to Hubris. Otherwise, stick to minor entities, natural forces, and representative characteristics they care to embolden/embody. Ancient Greeks were all about embodiment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T14:46:45-07:00","id":987949,"title":"","content":"Calling yourself Thrice-Great Hermes <i>would</i> seem a bit impious to the Ancients---even from another land, if they knew what you were claiming.<br /> <br /> <br /> There's a rather large difference between calling yourself &quot;The Great Thunderhand&quot; when your hero who held that title dies and calling yourself &quot;Liu Bu&quot;. The attitude of the ancients to those stealing names was pretty negative... and I mean in most cultures I've studied, not just western ones. Sure, the Mastigos are all about picking that sort of fight, but it seems pretty weird for an Obrimos to violate honesty norms, of all things.<br /> <br /> Taking noble or ruling names, though, has a very time honored tradition, especially when stepping into ceremonially significant roles. (say, becoming a noble, stepping up to rule a house, or even becoming a general) Changing one's name when adopted, as well, and I don't just mean just the patronymic.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest that taking Shadow names is ancient, but the sorts of names taken has shifted wildly and claiming the names of ancient figures of legend has increased over time, while choosing meaningful (for various mystical reasons) names that are more original or are descriptive titles has decreased. (See <i>Werewolf: The Forsaken</i> (or Apocalypse) and <i>Fullmetal Alchemist</i> for examples of what I'm saying.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T11:58:22-08:00","id":1033518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/987583-when-did-shadow-names-become-common?p=987949#post987949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd suggest that taking Shadow names is ancient, but the sorts of names taken has shifted wildly and claiming the names of ancient figures of legend has increased over time, while choosing meaningful (for various mystical reasons) names that are more original or are descriptive titles has decreased. (See <i>Werewolf: The Forsaken</i> (or Apocalypse) and <i>Fullmetal Alchemist</i> for examples of what I'm saying.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I still try to understand what you wrote in last post - could you eloborate on that? Best with some ancient Shadow Names of your thinking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T13:48:35-08:00","id":1033615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/987583-when-did-shadow-names-become-common?p=987617#post987617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>TLDR- </b>Even in the real world, Shadow Names are a thing for those who practice magic in their communities. The idea and the mantle of Practitioner of the Art as a separate person from Bob-who-knows-some-Magic go hand-in-hand as far back as anyone can tell, even to shamanistic cave drawings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wanted to like that post twice. +1 internet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/987583-when-did-shadow-names-become-common?p=987949#post987949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd suggest that taking Shadow names is ancient, but the sorts of names taken has shifted wildly and claiming the names of ancient figures of legend has increased over time, while choosing meaningful (for various mystical reasons) names that are more original or are descriptive titles has decreased. (See <i>Werewolf: The Forsaken</i> (or Apocalypse) and <i>Fullmetal Alchemist</i> for examples of what I'm saying.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this. As history grows plagiarism increases, that seems accurate to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-17-2017, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T09:04:09-08:00","id":1040021,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8573\" data-vbnamecard=\"8573\">Zombiecakes</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> What would be a good Shadow Name to use istead of Imhotep, but still covering roughly the same symbolism (that is, healing, construction, geomancy, sacred geometry, embalming etc. etc.)?<br /> <br /> Imhotep-shows-the-way or something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T14:13:39-08:00","id":1041474,"title":"","content":"Imhotep actually means, in Ancient Egyptian, &quot;one who comes in peace&quot;. But, if you want to go with what he is <i>known </i>for (and became god of) then Ptah is a good choice, especially since said god was rumoured to be Imhotep's father. There's also Kothar, the Levantine god who is somewhat analogous to Ptah. Nuwa is a Chinese goddess who was known for creating mankind, and repairing the Pillar of Heaven with five coloured stones representing the five base elements of the world, and she is occasionally depicted as a dragon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T11:06:39-08:00","id":1049376,"title":"","content":"Just to have a brief idea. How Shadow Names alter a person? Like, it's an accent? The hair/eye color can change? Or it's just some aura thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T11:25:49-08:00","id":1049384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/987583-when-did-shadow-names-become-common?p=1049376#post1049376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How Shadow Names alter a person? Like, it's an accent? The hair/eye color can change? Or it's just some aura thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither - Shadow Name is only your 'secret identity'. Only real magical things it does is that magic is not looking for 'Bob Ernst' ( and anyone connected to him ) but for 'Thor the Lightbearar' ( and anyone connected to him ), depending on your Wisdom. Other than that, Shadow Name Merit can give you nice Yantra to spellcasting if you would play 'Thor' for using spell.<br /> <br /> But you CAN deepen you Shadow Name with some color changing and acting - just like your any other, normal 'false identity'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-15-2017, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T16:33:10-08:00","id":1049564,"title":"","content":"Actually Shadow Names <i>does</i> change you, but the effects are probably more &quot;natural&quot; than spontaneous change of eye colour. Natural occurences that &quot;corrects&quot; the character in a way that is not overtly supernatural. But that's my take on it. What the book says is that Shadow Names that already have cultural associations will let those resonances and attachments seep into the character. For example someone with Odin as a Shadow Name has an increased risk of losing one eye. (p.292)<br /> That said there's nothing mechanically forcing a player's character to become more like their Shadow Name. I think it's up to the player to try to incorporate the persona (which is also grounds for increasing the Shadow Name Merit) into the roleplaying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}